{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4FromSpinIsospin_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4FromSpinIsospin_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L135-L145","doc":"**The class is inhabitable** — the complement of the theorem above, and the property\nthe predecessor provably lacked. Taking `W ≡ 1` forces `E_gate ≡ 0` by the capacity law,\nand `c ≡ B_AME / 0 = 0` by `div_zero`, so this data satisfies both laws.\n\nRecorded because \"no instance is provided\" must mean *the conjecture is open*, not *no\ninstance could exist*. Without this, the two statements are indistinguishable from\noutside. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4FromSpinIsospin_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4FromSpinIsospin_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L123-L133","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which neither the vacuous stub nor the uninhabitable\npredecessor was: with `E₀ = 1` and `W ≡ 1` the capacity law forces `E_gate ≡ 0`, so the\nconstant-one `E_gate` falsifies it.\n\nStated as a theorem because \"the carrier asserts something, and something that *can* be\nsatisfied\" is exactly the property both earlier versions lacked — in opposite directions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4_occupancy_via_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wignerSU4_occupancy_via_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L114-L121","doc":"**The occupancy in terms of the Plancherel weight alone** — derived by composing the\ntwo laws, rather than stated as a third field. This is what the block's pair of equations\namounts to, and it follows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.occupancy_from_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.occupancy_from_binding","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The empirical magic `A·8G` baseline is superseded by the dynamic occupancy\nrequirement `c_λ = B_AME / E_gate`, which captures ~94 % of the binding at the ⁴He\nmagic shell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.capacity_from_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.capacity_from_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The dynamic cluster capacity is dictated by the Plancherel weight `W A` of the SU(4)\nspin-flavour conjugate partition `λ ⊢ 3A`: `E_gate = E₀ · ln(1 / W_λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin.lean#L88-L108","doc":"**CONJECTURE (Wigner SU(4) closure).** The SU(4) = SU(2)_S × SU(2)_I spin-isospin\nsymmetry arises as the combined classical limit of the spin SO(3) fibre action (D10) and\nthe canonical isospin ℤ/2 swap (D9).\n\n`E_0` is the gate scale; `W`, `E_gate`, `B_AME` and `c` are families indexed by mass\nnumber `A`, all supplied by the **caller** — so the class is false for data that does not\nsatisfy the two laws (see `wignerSU4FromSpinIsospin_refutable`).\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as\n`[WignerSU4FromSpinIsospin E_0 W E_gate B_AME c]` and are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:wigner-su4-from-spin-isospin ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:wigner-su4-from-spin-isospin","label":"conj:wigner-su4-from-spin-isospin","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/wigner-su4-from-spin-isospin.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}